{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.MatrixSchurCommutant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MatrixSchurCommutant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Eigenspace.Triangularizable","lean:module:Mathlib.FieldTheory.IsAlgClosed.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MatrixSchurCommutant.commutant_scalar_of_irreducible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MatrixSchurCommutant.commutant_scalar_of_irreducible","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MatrixSchurCommutant.lean#L58-L84","doc":"**Matrix Schur's lemma.** Over an algebraically closed field, any matrix `A`\ncommuting with every generator `ρ s` of an *irreducible* representation is a\nscalar multiple of the identity. This is exactly the `schur` hypothesis of\n`invariantForm_proportional_of_commutantScalar` (#4160) — now a theorem, given\nirreducibility. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.MatrixSchurCommutant.IsIrreducibleRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.MatrixSchurCommutant.IsIrreducibleRep","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/MatrixSchurCommutant.lean#L52-L56","doc":"**Irreducibility of a matrix representation.** The only subspaces of `n → k`\ninvariant under every `ρ s` are `⊥` and `⊤`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}